# Cloudflare Pages redirect table.
#
# NOTE: `next.config.js` `redirects()` does nothing here. This is a static
# export (`output: 'export'`) — there is no Next server to run a redirect, so
# the config option is silently inert and the platform's own table is the only
# mechanism that works. Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output
# root; `public/` is copied verbatim, so it lands there.
#
# `formatPairs` drops any pair with zero models in common (see
# lib/utils/format-compare.ts) — there is nothing to compare when not one model
# in the index ships both formats, which is the case for GPTQ against AWQ and
# against EXL2. Those two URLs were real pages and are kept reachable rather
# than 404'd; `/formats/gguf-vs-gptq/` answers the merged question directly.
#
# The postbuild gate checks both halves of every line: the source must NOT be an
# exported page (or the redirect is shadowed and dead) and the target MUST be
# one (or the redirect points at a 404).
/formats/awq-vs-gptq/      /formats/gguf-vs-gptq/      301
/formats/exl2-vs-gptq/     /formats/gguf-vs-gptq/      301
/zh/formats/awq-vs-gptq/   /zh/formats/gguf-vs-gptq/   301
/zh/formats/exl2-vs-gptq/  /zh/formats/gguf-vs-gptq/   301
